WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.667
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.167
-Welcome to the show.
-And Michael.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.434
-Great to see you guys.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:08.133
Sean, you actually made your
network TV debut on

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.934
"Late Night,"
when I hosted "Late Night."

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.534
-I did. Right here.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:15.601
So, February 5, 2010.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.000
-Oh, really?
You remember the date?

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.701
-I'm very good with dates.
-How do you remember the date?

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:23.601
-So, two days later,
on February 7, 2010,

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:27.133
the New Orleans Saints, hometown
team, won the Super Bowl.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.367
-Ah. That's big deal.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.334
-So my appearance on
"Late Night"

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:36.200
was immediately forgotten
by everyone in my life,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.100
everyone in my hometown.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.300
I stood right there and, at the
end of my set, went, "Who dat?"

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.601
The battle cry of
the New Orleans Saints.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.067
No one remembered.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.033
-Oh, my God.
Well, here you are now.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.601
-It's great to be back.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.334
-Michael, it's always
good to see you, buddy.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.534
"SNL" was great, by the way,

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.267
with Steve Martin last weekend
and Martin Short.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:55.901
-Oh, man, wasn't that crazy?
-That was a great episode.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.133
This week, you have
Austin Butler and Lizzo.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.534
-Yes.
-That's going to be a good show.

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.167
-It's the Christmas show.
It's the most important one.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.868
-It's a big deal.
-Yeah, it's the one.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:06.200
-You produced Sean's special,
and I want to get into that.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.534
But, first, I have to talk
about something that I saw.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.634
I follow you on Instagram.
-Oh, I'm very sorry.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.367
-And -- No, no.
You always make me laugh.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.534
But I want to clarify something

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.133
that happened
between you and Questlove.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:19.400
-Oh, yeah.
We should talk about this.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.634
-So, the other week --

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:23.434
So, SZA was the musical guest
on "SNL," okay?

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.734
So, here's what Michael posted.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.267
-It says...

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.534
-That's right. I did.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.767
Sounds strange, but it happened.
-Natural.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:52.434
Obviously.
-She meant business.

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.100
-And, of course...

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:20.734
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:24.601
So, that's -- So, it's a
rock, paper, scissors joke,

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:25.801
a long walk.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:29.534
-It also really happened.
-Yeah, right.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.300
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.434
What a long walk
for that punch line,

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.067
which I love and I laughed at.

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:38.100
And I know you delete
your Instagrams

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.100
so they don't live forever.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.167
-Yeah.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.734
-But Questlove posted it
to preserve it.

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:43.801
-Yes.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:44.934
-Did you know
that Quest did that?

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.434
-I had no idea.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:50.567
What happened was, I found out
that they covered this story on

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:54.167
"The Breakfast Club"
as actual gossip.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:58.834
And they attached
Questlove's name to it,

00:02:58.834 --> 00:02:59.901
and I'm like, "What?!

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.100
When did this happen?"

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.467
-Look at this.
This is all the headlines.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.734
This is real. Look at these.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.400
"SZA arm-wrestled The Rock
at 'SNL.'

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.767
Questlove says, 'True story.'"

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.067
-Wait. What?!

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.701
-Questlove --

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.634
-Wait. They think I did that?
-Yeah.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.734
-They think,
like, you witnessed it.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:17.701
-Oh, no, I was
preserving your joke.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.434
-No, no, no.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:22.334
This is why I delete everything,
because people think it's real.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.267
-I just wanted to make
the record straight.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.200
Yeah, that did not happen.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.234
-Your posts are like the McRib.

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:31.200
You know?
-They're here for --

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.634
-They're here for a minute,
and then it's gone.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.200
-Yeah, just gone, yeah.
-When are they coming back?

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.601
-Yeah. When did you decide to do
a special together?

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:36.934
Michael, you produced it.

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.968
-Well, Sean is being a little
bit humble right now,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.868
but he always kind of had this
reputation in New York City.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.767
Anybody that follows
New York City comedy,

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:47.067
he always had this reputation of
being one of the killers,

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:50.601
like, just one of the absolute
beasts at it, you know?

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.767
So everyone kind of knew of
him that maybe even

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:57.200
he didn't know back,
and I was one of those people.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.234
-You can tell how comfortable
I am right now

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:01.634
having Michael say all this.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.901
Even though I appreciate it,
yeah, that -- Thank you.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.901
-But I always asked him --
I was like,

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.801
"Man, I would love to do
a special with you."

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:10.367
And he started producing --

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.234
You already produced one with
800 Pound Gorilla, right?

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.400
-800 Pound Gorilla, yeah.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.634
-And he was like,
"Man, I would love to, you know,

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.300
have you kind of,
you know, walk this in."

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.901
And I was absolutely on board.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.000
-Is that right?
Is that what you --

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.234
-This feels like we're married.

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:24.701
-Yeah, yeah.
-Is that how you remember it?

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:27.267
-I mean, it's --
Eh, you know, close.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.434
-How do you remember it?

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.033
-See, I remember more
we would --

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:33.167
We had this conversation
like a few years ago.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.300
I was like,
"I want to do a special."

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.334
And Michael -- We were --

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.834
You know,
we're at the Comedy Cellar.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.868
You're having some drinks.
You're having some fun.

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:40.534
And, suddenly,
he's like, "I'm doing it.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:41.868
I'm producing your special."

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.767
I say, "Great. Let's do it.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:46.367
I'm doing it and I'm running
the hour next week at the --

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:47.534
Come see it."

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.334
And he didn't show up.

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.834
But busy man, you know?
I understood.

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.033
-Yeah.
-No big deal.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.734
And then I see him
like a month or two later.

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:55.901
He's like, "Don't worry.
I want to do it.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.000
I want to produce it."

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.868
I'm like, "You got --
Let's do it."

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:01.467
And then a pandemic hits, right?
-Wow.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.601
-Oh, right. Yeah.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.000
-And then, you know,
that happens.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.300
-Alright, so that happened, too.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.767
-You kinda forget
every prior obligation you had

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:10.834
up until that point.

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:12.734
And then, finally,
we just did it.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.267
800 Pound Gorilla came to me
and said, "Let's do it."

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.567
I said, "Absolutely."

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:18.033
And then, one night,
I get a text from my manager,

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.534
who's like, "Hey,
I'm talking with Michael's reps.

00:05:20.534 --> 00:05:21.934
He's in.
He wants to produce it."

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:23.167
I'm so excited.

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:24.734
And then I see you
a couple months later,

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:27.968
and you're like,
"I'm mad at you."

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:29.801
You remember any of this?

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.234
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:32.801
-You were like,
"I'm mad at you, man.

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:34.033
You're doing this --
I hear you're doing a special.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.200
I want to produce it."

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.968
I'm like, "You are.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:40.367
I've been talking to
your entire --"

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:43.100
-Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.100
-"I've been talking
to your team.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.501
You're producing this."
-Yeah.

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.234
"You're taking this.
We're going to do it."

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:51.067
And you were like, "Oh, yep.
Sorry. Done.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:52.801
What do you want?"
-I said, "Streaming."

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:55.367
And you go, "Pssh! Got it."
And then you did it.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.467
-That's --
I forgot all about that.

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:58.934
-Yeah.

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:01.567
-I know you got to film it --
What's the beautiful theater?

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:04.801
-Oh, Tipitina's in New Orleans.
-Tipitina's.

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:07.400
-A classic, old -- It's, like,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.667
an amazing music venue
in the city.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.667
And I wanted to shoot it
in the city

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:13.868
where you knew it was in
New Orleans without --

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.033
You know,
I didn't want to put like,

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.367
"Hey, look,
a Mardi Gras float going by,"

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:17.467
or, like --

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.634
-You don't want to be too --
-No.

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.200
Like, "Hey, look,
we're all eating po' boys,

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.100
and, uh-oh,
a special is about to happen."

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.367
-Yeah, yeah,
you don't want to do that.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:24.801
You want to keep it subtle.
-Right, right.

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:26.734
-But even your accent.

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:28.300
Did you have more of
a New Orleans accent

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.234
before you were in the city?

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:34.000
-Oh, so, I often get inquired.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.968
People ask, where is my
New Orleans accent?

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:38.200
It's -- The thing
you're thinking about

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.300
that most people
think about when it comes to

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.567
a New Orleans accent, that like,

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:42.000
"Oh, you better watch out.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.501
They got -- We found a
12-foot gator on the lawn,

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:46.667
cut him open.

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.334
His belly full of live crawdads.

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:49.667
They was in there hiding.

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:51.133
-That's exactly right.
That's New Orleans.

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:54.567
-"Ooh, man, the other day, I got
pulled over by the sheriff,

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.267
and he was in a boat.

00:06:56.267 --> 00:06:58.000
I said, 'Sheriff, how you got
that boat on land?'

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.467
He said, 'I ain't on land, boy.

00:06:59.467 --> 00:07:01.000
You got your damn truck
in the bayou again.'"

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.400
-Yeah, exactly right.
That's exactly right.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.767
That's what we like.
-Right.

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:06.634
-That's a more
Western Louisiana.

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:10.200
Like, that's Lafayette,
you know, Thibodaux.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.767
-I was about to throw
beads at you.

00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:16.868
-I think, like,
a true New Orleans accent

00:07:16.868 --> 00:07:19.267
sounds far more
like an actual --

00:07:19.267 --> 00:07:20.334
like a New York accent.

00:07:20.334 --> 00:07:21.667
-Really?

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:24.400
-Like, if you took, like,
that New York guy who's like,

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.501
"Hey, you know, move it.

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:26.534
What are you doing?
Get out of my way.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:27.834
Where you going?
What do you want?

00:07:27.834 --> 00:07:29.367
Will you get out of my face?
What do you want from me?

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:30.901
I'm going my way. You go yours.
What?"

00:07:30.901 --> 00:07:36.067
Take that guy and give him
a few Valium, right?

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:39.467
And once those Valium take
effect, now you got, like,

00:07:39.467 --> 00:07:41.200
a legit New Orleans accent.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.367
Just sort of like,
"Where you going?

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:46.133
Ah, that's crazy. I'll come."

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:48.300
You know? "What you --"

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.567
Like, a true New Orleans
accent sounds far more like

00:07:51.567 --> 00:07:56.067
a sedated firefighter
from Brooklyn.

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:59.000
"Oh, they got a fire over there?
Aw, that's crazy, dude.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.167
Oh, I got to fight it?
Yeah, that's a'ight."

00:08:03.167 --> 00:08:06.133
-I want to show a clip.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:07.367
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:07.367 --> 00:08:08.834
By the way, I also want to say,

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:11.767
I love the length
of this comedy special.

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:15.667
I appreciate that as a fan of
comedy specials and comedians.

00:08:15.667 --> 00:08:17.067
This is like an hour and a half.

00:08:17.067 --> 00:08:18.734
-Hour and 27 minutes,
but there's a narrative.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.000
There's a story.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.667
-That's some quality comedy
you can watch right now.

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:24.667
Stream on Peacock right now.
I want to show a clip.

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:26.367
Here's Sean's special,
"Number One."

00:08:26.367 --> 00:08:27.634
Take a look.

00:08:27.634 --> 00:08:30.133
-My parents were born
the same year,

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:32.501
next door to one another
in the Lower Ninth.

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:35.133
They grew up
knowing each other since birth

00:08:35.133 --> 00:08:37.834
and they started dating
when they were like 14, okay?

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:42.467
And it ruined me. Destroyed me.

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:44.968
Their relationship
turned me into

00:08:44.968 --> 00:08:47.701
a little romance bitch,
you know?

00:08:47.701 --> 00:08:50.434
Just weeping all the time.

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:55.200
Like a fatter version of Cupid,
just firing hot-dog darts

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.167
that would just
deflect off of every woman

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:59.868
I fell in love with
every 48 hours.

00:08:59.868 --> 00:09:01.801
You understand?

00:09:01.801 --> 00:09:03.701
You think being ghosted is bad?

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:06.300
Try not getting a response to
hand-written poetry

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:10.167
over and over again.

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:12.300
-That's exactly right.
You think that's hard?

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:15.100
Michael Che, Sean Patton,
everybody.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.634
"Sean Patton: Number One" is
streaming right now on Peacock.

